
========================================================================================================
1.  THE GATE, AND THE ONE PROPERTY THAT MAKES THIS LEDGER NON-TRIVIAL
========================================================================================================

  G(omega) = 1/(1 + i omega/omega_c);   Re G = 1/(1 + (omega/omega_c)^2)  = RETAINED MI amplitude.
  omega_c in [1.78, 2.21]e-14 rad/s (canon) <-> a period of 9.01-11.18 Myr.
  EVERY MICROSCOPE frequency is 10^10-10^12 times ABOVE that corner, so the AC channel is gated OFF
  by ~20+ orders.  The whole informational value of this lane therefore sits in Fork C:
   [PASS] sympy: the 1-pole identity |G|^2 = Re G holds (residual 0)
   [PASS] Fork C: Re G(omega=0) = 1 for EVERY omega_c in the window (a low-pass gate cannot suppress a DC anomaly)

